# Accepted image CVEs for the Trivy gate in .github/workflows/ci.yml
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line. `#` starts a comment.
#
# RULES:
#   1. Every entry needs a reason and a review date. No bare IDs.
#   2. Adding a line here ships a known-vulnerable image. If you cannot justify
#      it in writing, fix it instead: rebuild on a newer base digest (the usual
#      fix for an OS-package CVE) or bump the Python dependency.
#   3. The CI gate already passes --ignore-unfixed, so anything reaching this
#      file HAS a released fix and is being consciously deferred. That is a
#      higher bar than "it's noisy".
#   4. Review at the stated date and delete the entry once the fix is in.
#
# The usual fix for an OS-level finding is NOT an entry here - it is refreshing
# the base image digest in the Dockerfile:
#
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect python:3.11-slim-bookworm
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CURRENT STATUS: nothing suppressed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This gate has not yet been run against a published image in CI - Trivy is not
# installed on the machine where this pipeline was authored, so the first real
# result will come from the first CI run. Expect Python-package findings
# matching those listed in .github/security/pip-audit-ignores.txt (starlette,
# python-multipart), since Trivy reads the same dist-info metadata.
#
# Do not pre-emptively add entries here to make that first run green. Read the
# findings, then decide.
